Upstream-Status: Pending
Exit: Drop when gnome-build-meta passes PREFIX to dnsmasq itself.
Subject: dnsmasq: install under %{prefix} instead of /usr/local

Overriding make-args with only BINDIR drops the make plugin's PREFIX, so
dnsmasq's Makefile default of /usr/local wins and its man page lands in
/usr/local/share/man. Pass PREFIX explicitly so it goes to %{mandir}.

diff --git a/elements/core-deps/dnsmasq.bst b/elements/core-deps/dnsmasq.bst
index 8e2c0917..288296a1 100644
--- a/elements/core-deps/dnsmasq.bst
+++ b/elements/core-deps/dnsmasq.bst
@@ -17,4 +17,4 @@ depends:
 - freedesktop-sdk.bst:public-stacks/runtime-minimal.bst
 
 variables:
-  make-args: BINDIR=%{sbindir}
+  make-args: PREFIX=%{prefix} BINDIR=%{sbindir}
